  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a radioactive sample, <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> nuclei either decay into stable <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> nuclei with decay constant <math><mn>4.5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math> per year or into stable <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> nuclei with decay constant <math><mn>0.5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math> per year. Given that in this sample all the stable <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> and <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> nuclei are produced by the <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> nuclei only. In time <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></math> years, if the ratio of the sum of stable <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> and <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> nuclei to the radioactive <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi></mrow><mrow><mn>19</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> nuclei is <math><mn>99</mn><mo>,</mo></math> the value of t will be : [Given <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.3</mn></math> ]<br ><img src=\"assets\\qt0008_e5e80c001655.png\"/></p>"
